WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.960
Two factors switch on the same receptor at the axon tip.

2
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.880
Why does a neuron need both?

3
00:00:09.883 --> 00:00:15.063
In the mouse, sympathetic axons grow out along blood vessels before reaching the

4
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:16.203
organs they innervate.

5
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.273
The vessels, an intermediate target, make NT-3.

6
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.693
The final targets make NGF.

7
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:25.973
Both factors can activate TrkA.

8
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:32.193
Kuruvilla, Ginty and colleagues gave each factor only to the distal axons of

9
00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:33.813
sympathetic neurons in culture.

10
00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:38.457
With NT-3 on the axon tips, do the axons grow?

11
00:00:39.377 --> 00:00:40.557
Do the cell bodies survive?

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.640
NT-3 supported local axon growth through TrkA.

13
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.160
But the cell bodies did not survive.

14
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.840
NGF supported both growth and survival.

15
00:01:00.816 --> 00:01:01.876
Why the difference?

16
00:01:03.016 --> 00:01:04.016
Trafficking.

17
00:01:04.516 --> 00:01:10.136
NGF and TrkA complexes were taken into the cell and carried back to the cell body.

18
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.110
NT-3 and TrkA complexes were not stably carried back.

19
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:19.283
So NT-3 switches the receptor on at the tip.

20
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:21.823
But that signal is not carried home.

21
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:24.063
It is not useless.

22
00:01:25.023 --> 00:01:30.263
In mice lacking NT-3, sympathetic axon growth and target innervation were impaired.

23
00:01:31.316 --> 00:01:33.376
The paper also proposed a handoff.

24
00:01:34.349 --> 00:01:40.069
Retrograde NGF signaling raises a second neurotrophin receptor, p75.

25
00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:45.529
As p75 rises, the neuron responds less to NT-3.

26
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:52.193
A factor that acts only locally can steer an axon.

27
00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:55.173
It cannot, by itself, keep the neuron alive.

28
00:01:56.216 --> 00:02:01.336
So competition for the final target depends on the trafficking of the receptor, not

29
00:02:01.336 --> 00:02:02.336
only on binding.

30
00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:05.729
Takeaway: binding at the tip is not enough.

31
00:02:06.989 --> 00:02:09.569
Survival needs a signal that makes it home able to signal.
